<!-- pole — the upright cylinder a grasp policy was trained on.

     Loaded through rtc_mujoco_sim's object_pool, which attaches the body named
     `object` from `<directory>/<name>/object.xml` and adds its freejoint. So
     this file carries NO joint and NO scene — only the body.

     GEOMETRY IS THE CONTRACT. Radius 0.04 m, height 0.15 m, and the body origin
     at the CYLINDER CENTRE. A pose observation is the pose of this origin, so a
     policy trained with a centre-origin object sees the right position only
     when the sim body's origin is also the centre. The obvious alternative — an
     origin on the bottom face, which is how a grasp record may describe the
     same object — puts every observation 0.075 m off along the object's axis,
     and the result still looks like an ordinary pose. That is why this is a
     primitive and not a mesh: `size="0.04 0.075"` is radius and HALF-height,
     centred by construction, with nothing to re-export or mis-scale.

     PHYSICAL PARAMETERS ARE NOT FROM THE TRAINING ASSET — that asset's mass and
     friction are not available here. `mass` is spelled out (rather than derived
     from a density) because it is the one number a sim-to-sim comparison is
     most likely to vary; friction and condim copy object_sim's collision class
     so this object behaves like every other pool candidate. -->
<mujoco model="pole">
  <worldbody>
    <body name="object">
      <geom name="pole" type="cylinder" size="0.04 0.075" mass="0.2"
            contype="1" conaffinity="1" condim="4" friction="1 0.5 0.01"
            rgba="0.85 0.55 0.20 1"/>
    </body>
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>
